Tom: Not really. I think success means doing something you love and doing it well.
Lucy: So money is not the most important thing to you?
Tom: No. For me, a happy family and a job I enjoy matter more than money.
Lucy: That makes sense. My uncle is a village nurse, not rich at all, but he feels successful.
Tom: Exactly. He helps others every day, and that is a kind of success too.
Lucy: I agree. Maybe success is different for each person.
Tom: Yes, and the most important thing is to find your own road to it.', 'Lucy 问 Tom 是否只有又富又有名才算成功;Tom 认为成功是做自己热爱并做得好的事;对他来说幸福的家庭和喜欢的工作比金钱更重要;Lucy 提到当乡村护士的叔叔虽不富有却觉得成功;两人一致认为成功因人而异,最重要的是找到自己通向成功的路。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Tom think success mainly means?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Doing something you love and doing it well.","Being rich and famous only.","Owning a big house.","Winning every prize."]},{"q":"What matters more to Tom than money?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A bigger car.","A happy family and a job he enjoys.","Becoming famous.","Travelling abroad."]},{"q":"Why does Lucy mention her uncle?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Because he feels successful by helping others, though not rich.","Because he is very rich.","Because he is famous on TV.","Because he wants a new job."]},{"q":"What do Lucy and Tom finally agree on?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only money brings success.","Success can be different for each person.","Success is the same for everyone.","Nobody can be successful."]},{"q":"What does Tom say is the most important thing?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To copy other people exactly.","To give up when it is hard.","To find your own road to success.","To care only about fame."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U1', 'sufe');
But studies show that something called grit matters even more.
A person with grit keeps working towards a goal for years, not just for days.
They treat life like a long marathon rather than a short race.
In the end, the habit of never giving up often decides who succeeds.', '许多人认为天赋是成功的关键;但研究表明一种叫''毅力''的品质更重要;有毅力的人会朝目标坚持数年,而非几天;他们把人生当作长跑而非短跑;最终,永不放弃的习惯常常决定谁能成功。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do many people believe is the key to success?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Money.","Luck.","Looks.","Talent."]},{"q":"According to studies, what matters even more?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Grit.","A high score.","Good clothes.","A famous teacher."]},{"q":"How long does a person with grit keep working towards a goal?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["For a few minutes.","For years.","For one day.","Never."]},{"q":"What does a person with grit treat life like?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A short race.","A quick game.","A long marathon.","A lazy holiday."]},{"q":"What often decides who succeeds in the end?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Being born rich.","Avoiding all hard work.","Having many friends.","The habit of never giving up."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U1', 'sufe');
Jack: Don''t worry too much. You have practised hard for weeks.
Mia: But what if I forget everything in front of the judges?
Jack: Take a few deep breaths before you start. That always calms me down.
Mia: Do you really think I have a chance?
Jack: Of course. Even great people felt afraid before big moments.
Mia: Thanks, Jack. You always know how to cheer me up.
Jack: Just do your best. Whatever happens, you should be proud of trying.', 'Mia 为明天的数学竞赛紧张,担心会失败;Jack 安慰说她已苦练数周;Mia 怕在评委面前忘光;Jack 建议开始前深呼吸几次来让自己镇定;并说连了不起的人在重要时刻前也会害怕;Mia 感谢 Jack 让她振作;Jack 让她尽力,无论结果如何都该为尝试而自豪。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why is Mia nervous?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Because of a maths competition tomorrow.","Because she lost her book.","Because she is ill.","Because she missed the bus."]},{"q":"What does Jack remind Mia she has done?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She has slept all week.","She has practised hard for weeks.","She has skipped her lessons.","She has given up."]},{"q":"What does Jack suggest doing before she starts?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Shouting loudly.","Running away.","Taking a few deep breaths.","Eating a big meal."]},{"q":"What does Jack say about great people?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They never work hard.","They are always calm.","They never compete.","They also felt afraid before big moments."]},{"q":"What does Jack tell Mia at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To do her best and be proud of trying.","To skip the competition.","To copy others'' answers.","To stop studying maths."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U1', 'sufe');
The first try is often the hardest, and many people stop too soon.
But those who keep going slowly learn from their mistakes.
Each failure teaches them something new and brings them closer to the goal.
So when you fail, do not lose heart; instead, start over and try again.', '几乎每一项伟大成就都来自多次失败;第一次尝试往往最难,许多人太早放弃;但坚持下去的人会慢慢从错误中学习;每一次失败都教会他们新东西,使他们更接近目标;所以当你失败时,别灰心,要重新开始再试一次。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does almost every great achievement come after?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A single easy day.","Many failures.","A lot of luck only.","No effort at all."]},{"q":"What do many people do too soon?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Win the prize.","Become famous.","Stop trying.","Help others."]},{"q":"What do those who keep going learn from?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Their money.","Their friends.","Their holidays.","Their mistakes."]},{"q":"What does each failure do, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It teaches something new and brings you closer to the goal.","It makes the goal disappear.","It wastes all your time.","It stops you forever."]},{"q":"What should you do when you fail?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Lose heart and quit.","Start over and try again.","Blame other people.","Forget your goal."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U1', 'sufe');
Anna: Thanks! First, I write my main points on small cards.
Ben: Just the main points, not every word?
Anna: Right. If you read every word, the talk sounds boring.
Ben: What else helps you?
Anna: I practise out loud many times, and I pause at full stops and commas.
Ben: That''s clever. Anything for the nerves?
Anna: Yes. Breathe slowly before you start, and speak to one friendly face at a time.', 'Ben 问 Anna 演讲为何总那么棒;Anna 说先把要点写在小卡片上;只写要点而非逐字;因为逐字读会很无聊;还会大声练习多次,并在句号逗号处停顿;对付紧张则是开始前慢慢呼吸,每次只对一张友善的面孔讲。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Anna write on her cards?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Every single word.","Other people''s names.","Her main points.","Nothing at all."]},{"q":"Why shouldn''t you read every word?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It takes no time.","It is against the rules.","Cards are too small.","The talk sounds boring."]},{"q":"Where does Anna pause when she speaks?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["At full stops and commas.","In the middle of words.","Never at all.","Only at the very end."]},{"q":"How does Anna deal with nerves?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She shouts loudly.","She breathes slowly before starting.","She runs away.","She skips the talk."]},{"q":"Who does Anna suggest speaking to at a time?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The whole crowd at once with eyes shut.","No one in the room.","One friendly face at a time.","Only the judges."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U1', 'sufe');
A small step taken every day adds up over time.
If you learn five new words a day, that is almost two thousand in a year.
The secret is not speed, but doing a little, again and again.
Be patient, keep going, and one day you will be surprised how far you have come.', '你不必做什么惊天动地的大事才能走向成功;每天迈出一小步,日积月累会很可观;如果每天学五个新词,一年就近两千个;秘诀不在快,而在一点一点反复地做;要有耐心,坚持下去,有一天你会惊讶自己走了这么远。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the passage say you do NOT have to do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Sleep every night.","Eat breakfast.","Talk to friends.","Do something huge to move towards success."]},{"q":"What adds up over time?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A small step taken every day.","A long holiday.","A single big jump.","A lucky win."]},{"q":"If you learn five new words a day, how many is that in a year?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["About fifty.","Almost two thousand.","About five hundred.","Exactly ten."]},{"q":"What is the secret, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Doing everything in one night.","Working only when you feel like it.","Doing a little, again and again.","Being the fastest of all."]},{"q":"What will happen if you keep going patiently?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["You will quickly give up.","Nothing will change at all.","You will forget your goal.","One day you will be surprised how far you have come."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U1', 'sufe');

